 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Condensed pro-etale Tate twists",
 "statement": "Let $\\ell$ be a prime and $X$ an arbitrary scheme, using the small pro-etale site of [def-weil-pbc-proetale-site]. Use the geometric coefficient pullback $p_X^*$ and internal module objects of [def-weil-pbc-condensed-e-module-category]. Let $\\underline{\\mathbf Z}_\\ell(S)=C(S,\\mathbf Z_\\ell)$ on profinite sets, and let $\\underline\\Omega$ be the condensed ring whose sections on $S$ are continuous maps with values in one finite intermediate extension of $\\mathbf Q_\\ell$ in $\\Omega=\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell$, as specified in [prop-weil-pbc-qbar-condensed-two-colimit]. Put $R_X=p_X^*\\underline{\\mathbf Z}_\\ell$ and $B_X=p_X^*\\underline\\Omega$; thus $B_X$ is exactly condensedRingObj (Profinite.padicAlgClRingObj ell) X. The ring map $R_X\\to B_X$ is the pullback of the inclusion $\\underline{\\mathbf Z}_\\ell\\to\\underline\\Omega$ through the bottom finite intermediate field $\\mathbf Q_\\ell$.\n\nFor every $n\\in\\mathbf N$, including $n=0$, let $F_n=R_X\\otimes_{\\mathbf Z}\\mu_{\\ell^n,X}$ be the free internal $R_X$-module on the abelian roots-of-unity sheaf of [def-pur-roots-of-unity-sheaf]. Here free means tensoring the abelian sheaf with the ring object, not the free module on its underlying set. Its transition $F_{n+1}\\to F_n$ is induced by the $\\ell$-th-power map on roots of unity. Define $T_X=\\varprojlim_{n\\in\\mathbf N^{op}}F_n$ in internal $R_X$-modules, and $L_X=B_X\\otimes_{R_X}T_X$ by extension of scalars. Use the inverse-limit and sheaf-tensor constructions of [def-pur-sheaf-inverse-limit, def-pur-sheaf-tensor-product] in these module categories.\n\nDefine $B_X(0)=B_X$ (the tensor unit), $B_X(d+1)=B_X(d)\\otimes_{B_X}L_X$ for $d\\in\\mathbf N$, and $B_X(-d-1)=\\mathcal Hom_{B_X}(B_X(d+1),B_X)$ using the internal Hom of [def-pur-sheaf-hom]. Define tateTwistDerived X ell m for every $m\\in\\mathbf Z$ to be this internal module $B_X(m)$ placed in degree zero of $D(\\operatorname{Mod}_{B_X})$. These are the actual constructions tateModuleLevel, tateModuleTransition, tateModuleSystem, tateModule, tateTwistOne, tateTwistNat, tateTwist and tateTwistDerived at the recorded upstream revision. No finite-field structure on $X$, invertibility hypothesis on $\\ell$ on $X$, choice of a trivialization, local-freeness theorem, or identification with the common-stage coefficient category is part of this definition.",
 "source": {
  "document": "coord/reports/maintenance/nt-target-smooth-purity-qbar.md",
  "place": "Verbatim source exhibit WeilConjectures/TateTwist/ProEtale.lean: coefficient map lines 79-108; levels, transitions and limit lines 119-144; scalar extension, signed powers and degree-zero inclusion lines 148-179. Git blob b26295f63a04264246319a1fd5f8b4f6421eb78c; SHA-256 b9554907baced298abbb0648fe084ac9eaffcf576c4e03e6f26a90ff3f0fff2f.",
